| `child_env.credential_value_patterns.<label>` | string | five patterns: an Authorization header, an HTTP authorization value, a JWT, an opaque token and a PEM private key | a label mapped to a Python regular expression | `scripts/child_env.py`; `scripts/run_make_target.py` | A copied value matching a pattern is refused, naming the variable and the label, never the value. Pattern compilation syntax, recursion and overflow faults refuse the policy, naming child_env.credential_value_patterns and the label without pattern or compiler text; child_exec exits CONFIG before any script body runs. | a credential a child needs: `child_env.credentialed_values` | always |
